#!/bin/sh
#
# Heron ASV: runs after PX4's modules have started (rcS sources <airframe>.post).
#
# PX4's online gyro calibration runs whenever the vehicle is disarmed and decides "still"
# from the gyro's variance alone. A disarmed boat that turns at a steady rate (drifting,
# coasting, towed, moved in the Gazebo GUI) has a quiet gyro, so the turn rate was taken
# for sensor offset: measured 0.86 rad/s "calibrated" away during a 49 deg/s turn. The
# heading then froze during the turn, spun backwards for 10 s after it, and stayed up to
# 160 degrees wrong until the boat had driven around for a minute. Smaller cases were
# saved as CAL_GYRO0_ZOFF and turned the heading at rest on every later boot.
# The simulated gyro has no offset to calibrate.
gyro_calibration stop
